    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups against sub-par arms. **Kyle Tucker** (77.58) stands as our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Robert Gasser and an optimal cleanup spot. He is closely followed by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67); the latter is an intriguing play at the top of the order, where his elevated xwOBA and favorable wind conditions at the park provide a high floor for Runs scored. **Andy Pages** also finds himself in a strong position (66.76) against Gasser, as the opponent's 5.63 xERA creates a perfect environment for our core outfielders to capitalize on volume and scoring opportunities.\n\nWhile the high-scoring options are clear, the roster construction remains sensitive to the difficulty of today's matchups. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73) remains in the lineup despite a daunting clash with the elite arm of Paul Skenes, whose 2.96 xERA drags down what would otherwise be a much higher daily efficiency score. **Nolan Schanuel** was the primary consideration for the bench, narrowly missing the cut with a 41.65 score; he was ultimately pushed out by the higher-upside profiles of our confirmed starters, combined with the difficulty of hitting against Nathan Eovaldi. As a final note of caution, owners should track lineup confirmation for **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Sam Antonacci**; the \"Lineup Pending\" status on these players introduces variability, and we must also account for the unfortunate rainout of **Gunnar Henderson**, which removes one of our primary offensive engines from the equation entirely. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** already sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, making it critical that **Nasim Nunez** and **Liam Hicks** provide efficient output to maintain our pace in the 5x5 categories.",
